      ],
      "flags": {},
      "order": 36,
      "mode": 0,
      "inputs": [],
      "outputs": [],
      "properties": {},
      "widgets_values": [
        "Pixel sprite + driving video -> sprite sheet (Wan 2.1 VACE 1.3B pose control, fast) - EXPERIMENTAL\n\nTested 24 Oct 2026: with full-size human skeletons VACE draws a human in the sprite's colours. Scale the\nskeletons to the sprite before relying on it.\n\n1. Pixel sprite (blue): native pixel art; output keeps its pixel size + palette. It is VACE's reference image.\n2. Driving video (blue): one person doing the motion, whole body visible, static camera. Read at 16 fps, up to\n   49 frames. SDPose turns it into skeletons, padded onto the sprite's canvas.\n3. VACE draws the sprite following the skeletons. 8 steps, CFG 1.0, CausVid LoRA\n   (CC-BY-NC-4.0, non-commercial: bypass it and use ~20 steps, CFG 5, uni_pc for a commercial build).\n4. Re-pixelate \"height_match\" scales the clip once so the first frame has the sprite's height.\n5. RIFE x2 doubles the frames before Re-pixelate; Ctrl+B the yellow RIFE node to skip it.\nSaved to output/pixel/: sprite_from_video_vace_*.png (sheet), .json (Aseprite), .webp, _raw.mp4."
      ],
      "title": "READ ME"
    }
